   1:Core/Src/app/encoder.c **** /**
   2:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * @file    encoder.c
   3:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * @brief   Rotary encoder + push-button via TIM3 encoder mode.
   4:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  *
   5:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * EC11E15244G1 gives 2 counts/detent in TI12 (x4) mode — divide by 2.
   6:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * Requires .ioc: TIM3 EncoderMode = TIM_ENCODERMODE_TI12.
   7:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  *
   8:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * The push-button (PC0) is edge-driven via EXTI0: the .ioc still declares
   9:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * PC0 as plain GPIO_Input, Encoder_Init() re-configures it as an interrupt
  10:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * source at runtime so the generated MX_GPIO_Init() never needs touching.
  11:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  * The EXTI0_IRQHandler lives in the USER CODE section of stm32f4xx_it.c.
  12:Core/Src/app/encoder.c ****  */
